{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q20707684","formula":"C₁₃H₁₆ClNO","hill":"C13H16ClNO","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":16.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Arketamine","uk":"Аркетамін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Arketamine (developmental code names PCN-101, HR-071603), also known as (R)-ketamine or (R)-(−)-ketamine, is the (R)-(−) enantiomer of ketamine. Similarly to racemic ketamine and esketamine, the (S)-(+) enantiomer of ketamine, arketamine is biologically active; however, it is less potent as an NMDA receptor antagonist and anesthetic and thus has never been approved or marketed for clinical use as an enantiopure drug. Arketamine is currently in clinical development as a novel antidepressant.","uk":"Аркетамін (англ. Arketamine), кодові назви розробки PCN-101 , HR-071603, також відомий як (R)-кетамін або (R)-кетамін, є (R)-енантіомером кетаміну. Подібно до рацемічного кетаміну та ескетаміну, S(+)-енантіомера кетаміну, аркетамін є біологічно активним; однак він є менш потужним як антагоніст рецепторів NMDA та анестетик, і тому ніколи не був схвалений або використовувався в клініці як окремий препарат."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":644025,"mass":237.72,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN[C@]1(CCCCC1=O)C2=CC=CC=C2Cl","inchikey":"YQEZLKZALYSWHR-CYBMUJFWSA-N","iupac":"(2R)-2-(2-chlorophenyl)-2-(methylamino)cyclohexan-1-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"644025","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.089,"y":-2.37,"z":0.874,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.787,"y":-1.884,"z":1.003,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.667,"y":-1.46,"z":-1.425,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.738,"y":-0.293,"z":-0.526,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.592,"y":0.78,"z":-1.251,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.972,"y":1.958,"z":-0.348,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.751,"y":1.474,"z":0.872,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.549,"y":-0.71,"z":0.718,"el":"C"},{